    "title": "Memphis baseball assistant Ford Pemberton hired as ULM head coach - NewsBreak",
    "text": "Memphis baseball assistant coach Ford Pemberton has been hired as head coach at Louisiana-Monroe, the Warhawks announced June 11. Pemberton spent the past two seasons as the Tigers' hitting and infield coach and recruiting coordinator under coach Matt Riser. Prior to joining Riser's staff at Memphis , Pemberton also worked for Riser at Southeastern Louisiana. \"We look forward to building and working with a staff in putting together a championship club and aim to play a brand of baseball that Northeast Louisiana, the city of Monroe, the university, fans and alumni will all be proud of,\" Pemberton said in a news release. Pemberton, a native of Bossier City, Louisiana, succeeds Michael Federico, who resigned May 17 after eight seasons as the Warhawks' coach. Federico also has ties to Memphis. He spent five seasons (2004-08) with the Tigers as the pitching coach. Riser was hired at Memphis prior to the 2024 season. Since then, the Tigers are 45-65 overall and 18-36 in AAC play. \"Pem was my right-hand man for years and played a vital role in building a championship program,\" Riser said in a news release. \"He has a sharp baseball mind, unmatched work ethic, and an unshakable will to win. His relentless drive will serve him well, and he will lead Warhawk baseball to new heights.\" Reach sports writer Jason Munz at jason.munz@commercialappeal.com, follow him @munzly on X, and sign up for the Memphis Basketball Insider text group . This article originally appeared on Memphis Commercial Appeal: Memphis baseball assistant Ford Pemberton hired as ULM head coach",
